<Wiki
  title="Getting started"
  description="Create a PUV project, pin PHP, add Packagist packages, and run them without the system PHP."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>Getting started</h1>
  <p>
    This is the path from an empty directory to a running file. Install is the
    <a href="/wiki/install">previous page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Create the project</h2>
  <pre class="block">mkdir my-tool
cd my-tool
puv init
puv use 8.4</pre>
  <p>
    <code>puv init</code> writes <code>puv.toml</code>, <code>src/main.php</code>, and a
    <code>.gitignore</code> that ignores <code>.puv/</code> and <code>dist/</code>. The PHP line
    is your global pin, or <code>8.4</code> if you have none. A second <code>init</code> stops
    unless you pass <code>--force</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>puv use 8.4</code> writes that minor line into the manifest and downloads the highest
    matching patch if it is not installed. <code>puv use --global 8.4</code> sets the pin for
    shells that are not inside a project.
  </p>

  <h2>The manifest</h2>
  <pre class="block">[project]
name = "my-tool"
php = "8.4"

[dependencies]
symfony/console = "^7.0"

[dev-dependencies]
phpunit/phpunit = "^11.0"

[scripts]
build = "php build.php"
test = "phpunit"

[package]
format = "phar"
entrypoint = "src/main.php"</pre>
  <p>
    <code>php = "8.4"</code> is a minor line. The lockfile stores the patch under
    <code>[runtime]</code>, so a later sync does not float to a newer 8.4 by itself.
  </p>

  <h2>Add a package</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv add symfony/console
puv add symfony/console:^7.0
puv add --dev phpunit/phpunit</pre>
  <p>
    With no constraint, PUV resolves the highest stable release and writes a caret of that
    major.minor. On 4 Oct 2026 that was <code>symfony/console ^8.1</code> and
    <code>phpunit/phpunit ^13.4</code>. The constraint you pass is the one that is written.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>add</code> edits <code>puv.toml</code>, resolves, writes <code>puv.lock</code>, and
    installs into <code>.puv/</code>. Package bytes live once, under
    <code>~/.cache/puv/packages/</code>, addressed by SHA-256. The project only symlinks them.
  </p>

  <h2>Run</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv run src/main.php
puv src/main.php
puv -c 'echo PHP_VERSION;'
puv run phpunit</pre>
  <p>
    <code>puv src/main.php</code> is <code>puv run src/main.php</code>. Both prepend the
    generated autoloader, so the script does not <code>require vendor/autoload.php</code>.
    There is no <code>vendor/</code> directory. Dev tools land in <code>.puv/bin</code>, and
    <code>php</code> on that <code>PATH</code> is the managed runtime.
  </p>
  <p>
    Argument order for <code>puv run</code>: an existing file, then a name in
    <code>[scripts]</code>, then a project-local tool, then <code>.puv/bin</code>, then the
    command itself.
  </p>

  <h2>Lock and sync</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv lock
puv lock --upgrade
puv lock symfony/console
puv sync
puv install</pre>
  <p>
    <code>puv lock</code> rewrites the lock. It prefers versions already locked, unless you
    pass <code>--upgrade</code> or name one package. <code>puv sync</code> and
    <code>puv install</code> with no arguments install exactly <code>puv.lock</code>. If
    <code>puv.toml</code> changed, they stop and tell you to lock. They do not resolve on
    their own.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>puv remove symfony/console</code> drops the dependency from the manifest, locks
    again, and syncs.
  </p>

  <h2>Check, build, package</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv check
puv build
puv run build
puv package
puv package --format zip</pre>
  <p>
    <code>puv check</code> parses project PHP with tree-sitter and reports a drifted lock, a
    missing runtime, a missing extension, a missing entrypoint, and a script that points at a
    file that is not there. Deprecated constructs for the pinned minor line are warnings.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>puv build</code> syncs, then runs the <code>build</code> script if you declared one.
    It exports <code>PUV_BUILD=1</code>. <code>puv run build</code> is only that script, without
    the pipeline and without the variable.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>puv package</code> writes <code>dist/&lt;name&gt;.phar</code> by default. Dependencies
    are inside the archive. The PHP runtime is not. <code>--format zip</code> and
    <code>--format tar</code> write the same tree without a PHAR stub.
  </p>

  <h2>A Composer tree you already have</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv contain
puv sync</pre>
  <p>
    <code>contain</code> reads <code>composer.json</code> and <code>composer.lock</code> and
    writes <code>puv.toml</code> plus <code>puv.lock</code> from the locked graph. It does not
    delete the Composer files. <code>puv contain --clean</code> does, and only then. Plugins and
    <code>@composer</code> scripts are skipped and listed. Details are on the
    <a href="/wiki/scope">scope</a> page.
  </p>
</Wiki>
